# Runbook §6.1 — generated outputs and evidence must not appear as
# untracked files after the gate (bin/session-01-check.sh step 1).

.generated/*
!.generated/.gitkeep

evidence/*
!evidence/.gitkeep

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Session 2 operator inputs. These name a real host, real DNS, and a real
# provider organization, so only the redacted *.example.yaml forms are
# committed (runbook Session 2 §5.4).
#
# They are ignored rather than merely untracked because bin/session-01-check.sh
# step 1 fails on ANY untracked file, and these files live in the checkout on
# the deployment host where that gate also runs.
#
# Listed individually rather than as /project.*.yaml on purpose: a glob would
# silently hide a future project.third.example.yaml that ought to be committed.
/host.yaml
/capabilities.yaml
/project.alpha.yaml
/project.beta.yaml

# Deployed documents an operator installs from the host to run `--mode external`.
#
# **Two of these were tracked for six sessions** (D730). `alpha-outputs.json` and
# `beta-outputs.json` sat in the repository root at `schema_version` 10,
# `deployed_through_session` 6, observed 2026-08-15 — and they did not validate
# against the current schema at all. Four operator guides name them as the path
# to pass to `--project-a-outputs`, so an external run from a fresh checkout
# measured a Session 6 deployment while believing it measured the current one.
# `MUST_AGREE` on `source_commit` refuses the merge, which is four steps from the
# cause.
#
# Ignored rather than merely deleted: the file an operator installs has this name
# by convention, and a stale observation in source control has the shape of the
# real thing under a filename that reads as current.
/*-outputs.json
